  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -127,3 +127,29 @@ AdaptiveToolButton {\n AdaptiveToolButton::menu-indicator {\n     image: none;\n }\n+\n+/* -------------------------------------------------------------------\n+ * On KDE (Breeze), QMenuBar and QToolBar do not respect the standard\n+ * QPalette::Window by default in order to have the colors match that\n+ * of the window title bar, which is set by the KDE theme. That doesn't\n+ * look good, especially when the QToolBars contain other widgets that\n+ * are affected by our theme. Actually changing the title bar color to\n+ * match our theme from KDE is possible but more difficult. Also note\n+ * KDE uses different colors for active and inactive by default, which\n+ * is not accessed via the built-in access to the QPalette in QT\n+ * stylesheets but we might be able to get that from our themes.\n+ * ------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n+QMenuBar, QToolBar{\n+    background-color: palette(window);\n+}\n+\n+QMenuBar::item{\n+    color: palette(window-text);\n+}\n+\n+QMenuBar::item:selected{\n+    background-color: palette(highlight);\n+    color: palette(highlighted-text);\n+}\n+\n+/* XXX - QMenuBar::item:pressed ? */\n",
